WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
♪ [music] ♪

00:00:06.025 --> 00:00:08.923
[narrator] Give me a minute,
I'll show you how Cloud Firestore

00:00:08.924 --> 00:00:10.233
can help build apps quickly

00:00:10.233 --> 00:00:12.555
by simplifying data storage in the cloud.

00:00:12.888 --> 00:00:15.836
Cloud Firestore is a serverless
NoSQL document database

00:00:15.836 --> 00:00:18.453
that simplifies storing,
syncing, and querying data

00:00:18.453 --> 00:00:21.488
for your mobile, web,
and IoT apps at global scale.

00:00:21.722 --> 00:00:24.723
It simplifies app development
providing built-in security,

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:27.455
automatic scaling,
and multi-regional replication.

00:00:27.648 --> 00:00:28.933
It works in near real-time,

00:00:28.933 --> 00:00:32.493
allowing you to fetch changes
from your backend as they happen,

00:00:32.493 --> 00:00:35.056
which means you can collaborate
with multiple users

00:00:35.057 --> 00:00:37.755
and keep your data in sync
across multiple devices.

00:00:38.022 --> 00:00:41.256
It offers robust client libraries
and built-in offline support,

00:00:41.257 --> 00:00:42.889
so your app remains responsive,

00:00:42.889 --> 00:00:46.204
regardless of network latency
or internet connectivity.

00:00:46.622 --> 00:00:50.189
Cloud Firestore integrates
with both Google Cloud and Firebase.

00:00:50.189 --> 00:00:54.015
Creating it as simple as selecting
the location for your database,

00:00:54.015 --> 00:00:56.679
creating a collection,
and then adding documents to it,

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:59.922
leading to nested collections
and documents per your need.

00:01:00.188 --> 00:01:01.782
Accessing data is easy.

00:01:01.782 --> 00:01:04.256
You drill down into a collection,
and then a document

00:01:04.257 --> 00:01:05.888
until you get the data you want.

00:01:06.222 --> 00:01:09.622
Cloud Firestore allows you
to directly connect your app to the data,

00:01:09.855 --> 00:01:12.659
run strong transactions
across hundreds of documents,

00:01:12.659 --> 00:01:15.952
and run sophisticated queries
without worrying about performance.

00:01:16.288 --> 00:01:18.056
It comes with a generous [feature],

00:01:18.057 --> 00:01:21.755
and it's easy to estimate budget
since you pay per <i>read</i> and <i>write</i>.

00:01:22.055 --> 00:01:25.623
For all these reasons, Cloud Firestore
is perfect for cloud-native apps,

00:01:25.624 --> 00:01:27.155
including mobile, web,

00:01:27.156 --> 00:01:29.953
multi-user gaming apps, IoT, and more.

00:01:30.224 --> 00:01:33.713
So, next time you're thinking about
NoSQL document database for your apps,

00:01:33.824 --> 00:01:35.789
take a minute and look at Firestore.

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:39.255
For more info, check out
<i>cloud.google.com/firestore.</i>

